    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.completion, mini.pairs\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nI'm trying to find a way to remap `<cr>` with what is written in mini.completion help. But when doing so, the mini.pairs `<cr>` remapping is lost so doing enter inside pairs don't work anymore. How can I make the two plugins integrate nicely together on `<cr>` ?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.completion, mini.pairs</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm trying to find a way to remap <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;cr&gt;</code> with what is written in mini.completion help. But when doing so, the mini.pairs <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;cr&gt;</code> remapping is lost so doing enter inside pairs don't work anymore. How can I make the two plugins integrate nicely together on <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;cr&gt;</code> ?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.completion, mini.pairs\nQuestion\nI'm trying to find a way to remap <cr> with what is written in mini.completion help. But when doing so, the mini.pairs <cr> remapping is lost so doing enter inside pairs don't work anymore. How can I make the two plugins integrate nicely together on <cr> ?",
