                    "replyTo": {
                        "databaseId": 12246994,
                        "id": "DC_kwDOFoksYM4Aut_S",
                        "url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1585#discussioncomment-12246994"
                    },
                    "resourcePath": "/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1585#discussioncomment-12247271",
                    "updatedAt": "2025-02-19T08:56:05Z",
                    "upvoteCount": 0,
                    "url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1585#discussioncomment-12247271"
                },
                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> Ok. I have found where the problem come from. I was doing my remap inside the now function of mini.deps and was calling the setup function of mini.pairs in later. So my remap was overwritten by mini.pairs remap of `<cr>`.\r\n\r\nOh, yeah, that's a good point. The 'mini.pairs' probably should not remap `<CR>` if it is already mapped by the user. Either silently or with a warning. I'll take a look.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Ok. I have found where the problem come from. I was doing my remap inside the now function of mini.deps and was calling the setup function of mini.pairs in later. So my remap was overwritten by mini.pairs remap of <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;cr&gt;</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Oh, yeah, that's a good point. The 'mini.pairs' probably should not remap <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;CR&gt;</code> if it is already mapped by the user. Either silently or with a warning. I'll take a look.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Ok. I have found where the problem come from. I was doing my remap inside the now function of mini.deps and was calling the setup function of mini.pairs in later. So my remap was overwritten by mini.pairs remap of <cr>.\n\nOh, yeah, that's a good point. The 'mini.pairs' probably should not remap <CR> if it is already mapped by the user. Either silently or with a warning. I'll take a look.",
                    "createdAt": "2025-02-19T09:07:46Z",
                    "createdViaEmail": false,
                    "databaseId": 12247402,
